Z||000004||DaRkLoRD||10-11-1999||04:59 PM||||I always thought it'd be cool to design my own dash.. Check this page out for a bit of info on doing this.<P> <A HREF="http://www.perigee.net/~lunapark/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.perigee.net/~lunapark/</A> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.perigee.net/~lunapark/Dash/dash14a.jpg"> <P>I wouldn't have the instruments in the center tho, but I would like digital.. maybe some green ones.. blue would be awesome, but blue LEDs are a bit expensive I hear..||||reg||1
Z||000005||DJRice||10-12-1999||08:39 AM||||I like the PISA dash, but the one with the gauges in the center is a bit odd.  I guess there is something to be said for creating your own, but I dont like that one.<P>And For $1000+, I would keep my Original Plain Dash....||||reg||1
Z||000006||DaRkLoRD||10-12-1999||11:06 AM||||I don't particularly like that dash either, but I do like the page because it shows basically how to fabricate a custom dash.<P>I bet you could build that dash for far less than $1,000 tho, not including the speakers and gauges.||||reg||1
Z||000007||mwbackus||10-12-1999||03:33 PM||||Heres an interior that might not be too bad, its only $760 too..<BR> <A HREF="http://www.v8archie.com/parts.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.v8archie.com/parts.htm</A> <P>Mike||||reg||1
Z||000008||mrfixit58||10-12-1999||04:24 PM||||The V-8 Archie's isn't too bad but it would probablu cost you at least the difference ($250) just to cover the dash and arm rests.<BR>THe gauges look a lttle shrouded as well. Tall people may have to lean over to see the gauges.<BR>||||reg||11
Z||000009||mwbackus||10-12-1999||11:36 PM||||Just wanted to point out that the Pisa dash does not even come with door panels or a replacement console, they add another $595 for the door panels. I am sure that for much less than $800, one could probably upholster the entire Archie interior kit quite nicely.  It does appear to be a bit more work to obtain the finished product, but it is also a more radical change in overall appearance than Pisa dash.  I have not really taken the visibility issue into consideration, you have a valid point there.  It would be nice to see the finished product firsthand, a much better determination of the visibility issues could be made.  I am only 5' 9", so I am sure I would not be able to evaluate this as well our taller members. :-)<P>Mike||||reg||1
Z||000010||DaRkLoRD||10-13-1999||01:20 AM||||I know, I know.. it's a Ford.. but I really love the inside of this car. (Ford Probe GT, 1995 or 1996 I believe.)<P>Assuming it's possible to move the e-brake to the center console, I think it should be possible to create a Fiero interior that looks something like this. opinions?<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/probe_interior2.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by DaRkLoRD (edited 10-13-1999).]||||reg||1
Z||000011||mrfixit58||10-13-1999||07:29 AM||||The Probe interior is a nice one. It reminds me of a picture I just saw in a car mag that showed a 3rd generation Camaro that the owner installed a 4th generation dash. It looked great. Looks like a ton of work.||||reg||14
Z||000012||Carrolles||10-14-1999||06:40 PM||||A friend in St. Louis installed a NorthStar and the Pisa dash.  He said the Northstar was great.  The Pisa dash was poorly built and had to be trimmed a lot to make it fit.  The A/C duct registers were a mess to get installed and looking good.||||reg||1
Z||000013||DJRice||10-15-1999||08:39 AM||||Is it me or do those seats in the probe look suspiciously like something we could modify and use in our Fieros?||||reg||1
